#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:2
msgid "Creating a project from a private repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/shared/admonition-rtd-business.rst:2
msgid ""
"This feature is only available on `Read the Docs Business "
"<https://app.readthedocs.com/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:6
msgid ""
"On |com_brand|, projects can be connected to both private and public "
"repositories. There are two methods you can use to create a project from "
"a private repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:9
msgid "`Automatically create a project from a connected repository`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:10
msgid ""
"If you have a |git_providers_or| service connected to your account, "
"projects can be created automatically from a connected private "
"repository. We will handle the configuration of your repository to allow "
"cloning and pushing status updates to trigger new builds for your "
"project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:15
msgid "We recommend this method for most projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:17
msgid "`Manually create a project from a repository`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:18
msgid ""
"If your Git provider is unsupported or if your Read the Docs account is "
"not connected to your provider, you can still manually create a project "
"against a private repository. You will have to manually configure your "
"Git provider and repository after project creation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:23
msgid "Automatically create a project from a connected repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:28
msgid ""
"If your Read the Docs account has a connected |git_providers_or| account,"
" you should be able to automatically create a project from your "
"repository. Your account will need sufficient permissions to the "
"repository to automatically configure it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:32
msgid ""
"We recommend most users follow our :doc:`directions on automatically "
"creating projects </intro/add-project>` from a connected repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:35
msgid "Manually create a project from a repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:37
msgid ""
"In the case that automatic project creation isn't supported or doesn't "
"work for your repository, projects may be able to be manually created and"
" configured. You can still clone the repository with SSH but you will "
"have to manually configure the repository SSH keys and webhooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:44
msgid ":doc:`/guides/setup/git-repo-manual`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:45
msgid ""
"An overview of all of the steps required to manually add a project. This "
"guide is useful for both projects using public and private repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:49
msgid "Creating a project manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:51
msgid "Select an organization team to create the project in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:56
msgid "Select :guilabel:`Add project` from the main dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:57
msgid "Select :guilabel:`Configure manually` and then :guilabel:`Continue`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:58
msgid ""
"Select the organization team you'd like to create the project for. You "
"must be on a team with ``admin`` permission to do this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:61
msgid ""
"In the next form page you will manually configure your project's "
"repository details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:63
msgid "Specify your project and repository configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:68
msgid ""
"In the :guilabel:`Repository URL` field, provide the repository's SSH or "
"Git URL. This URL usually starts with ``git@...``, for example "
"``git@github.com:readthedocs/readthedocs.org.git``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:70
msgid ""
"Click :guilabel:`Next`, select :guilabel:`Build on Read the Docs`, and "
"follow the instructions to add a :doc:`configuration file </config-"
"file/index>` to your repository. The project uses your repository's "
"default branch, you can change it later in the :guilabel:`Default branch`"
" field of your project's :menuselection:`Settings`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/creating-project-private-repository.rst:74
msgid ""
"The project's first build should fail to clone your repository. This is "
"expected, your repository is not configured to allow access yet."
msgstr ""

